    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "DSA_TRACE_TREE",
      "narration": "One line to be careful about, and this is the bug people genuinely ship. We save current colon in brackets, not current. In Python a list is a reference: a whiteboard, not a photograph. Saving current itself would leave every entry pointing at the same whiteboard, and since backtracking keeps wiping that whiteboard, you'd finish with eight identical empty lists. The colon makes a copy. Four characters, and without them the function silently produces nonsense.",
      "durationFrames": 868,
      "timingSource": "tts",
      "background": "zoneC",
      "data": {
